<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$74 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$74 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian commercial paper market ended the week with a total of A$74 million worth of promissory notes sold at tender.</p>
<p>The Australian subsidiary of French telecommunications equipment, cabling, power and rail transport group, Alcatel Alsthom, made the largest issue, selling A$35 million of its paper at two basis points over bill.</p>
<p>The physical bank bill yield curve continued to flatten as hopes of a near-term easing in offical interest rates waned.</p>
<p>&quot;We'll continue to see that (flattening) unless something happens in the U.S. tonight,&quot; one dealer said.  </p>
<p>Australian debt markets remain nervous following a slide in U.S. Treasuries ahead of U.S. non-farm payrolls data due later on Friday.</p>
